From a55b83fbe2accab554a5dd7f90ee81f07cdd9bbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nonagenticai <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:19:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(metal): bound materializing SDPA prefill by chunking the
 query axis

sdpa_query_chunk_within_budget returned early on non-CUDA builds, so the
score-matrix chunk gate could only ever fire on CUDA. Metal has the same
materialization: MLX's fused SDPA declines an array-mask call at head_dim
256 on pre-M5 GPUs (#2621/#2646), and the fallback then forms the full
[B, H, q_len, k_len] scores. On a 48 GiB M4 Pro a 26,602-token prefill asks
Metal for 26,602^2 * 24 * 2 B = 33.97 GB in one buffer, past the 30.15 GB
per-buffer cap, so the request fails at the eval boundary.

Ask MLX's own fused-vs-fallback verdict through the existing probe (reusing
window_sdpa's per-thread memo) and let the existing, parity-tested
chunked_query_attention bound the transient. MLXCEL_METAL_ATTENTION_CHUNK=0
restores the old route. The build-metallib overlay is local-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
